  "details": "this is most likely more of a networking issue. \nwhen switching users ownership a few of the ondeserialized events will have a old url being received instead of the new owners url.\n it feels like a few of the deserialized events that the user was receiving when taking ownership is being processed later after they loose ownership, instead of having then discarded.\nis reproducible here: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_0c0b7b2c-b76e-4ae1-a2b3-7c2ae77784fc  \nhave the master put in a url(loads fine). have a second user load a new url(loads fine). then when the master loads a new url again, the second user will receive the first url for a second then start receiving the new url.\ndue to trying to load the url as it changes this will cause problems for alot of users. it will start to load the old url and as its loading the new url has arrived and tries to switch to it. but since the first url isnt done loading nothing will happen trying to load the new url.",
